ated with power, refused to hand over the image. He summoned a goldsmith and ordered him to make from the image a nine-strand necklace and anklet-bells for his horse, for his wife.\\\"}]\\n25:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"8\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"As soon as the goldsmith attempted to break the image on the king's order, the buzzing of hundreds of bees filled the air with dread. Terrible clouds gathered in the sky. Invisible strikes rained down upon the army. Elephants and horses began to die. Many soldiers began to perish.\\\"}]\\n26:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"9\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"The subjects too began urging the king to release the image. Suddenly Ghazikhan collapsed, seized by unbearable pain throughout his body. Utterly terrified, the king consented to hand over the image. He installed it upon a throne and worshipped it with great honour, then handed it over to the sangh. With joy and enthusiasm the sangh brought the image to Bhinmal and installed it amid great celebration. Everyone completed their vows of abstinence. The five sons of the wicked Subedar of Bhinmal, who had given Ghazikhan the false counsel, all died together.\\\"}]\\n27:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"10\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"In V.S. 1662, Sheth Varjang built a magnificent temple with a nine-chowk hall and circumambulatory path. The image of Parshwanath was installed on the full-moon day of Kartik. Because it delivered the people from fear of the king, this image became famous under the name Bhaybhanjan (\\\\\\\"Destroyer of Fear\\\\\\\"). In V.S. 1671 another temple, of Shri Chandraprabhaswami, was built here. Worshipping this Lord Parshwanath frees people from fear.\\\"}]\\n28:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"11\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"Other Temples: There are 8 more temples in the city and 2 outside it, all dating from the 14th to the 18th centuries. A new temple has been built in Bhinmal — the \\\\\\\"Shri Lakshmi Vallabh Parshwanath 72 Jinalaya Mahatirth\\\\\\\" — a very beautiful and artistic temple built on 100 acres of land. The Lord's image was installed here in February 2011.\\\"}]\\n29:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"12\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"Art and Sculpture: The ruins of old buildings in this ancient and famous city of Bhinmal are full of artistry. There are many ancient temples here with artistic images, truly delightful to behold.\\\"}]\\n2a:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"13\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"Directions: Bhinmal railway station is 1 km away, on the Bhildi–Jalore railway line. Dharamshala and bhojanshala facilities are available here, along with a treasure trove of Jain manuscripts. Bus service and private vehicles are available from Jalore and Sirohi.\\\"}]\\n2b:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"14\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"Scripture References: This shrine is mentioned in \\\\\\\"Nishidh Churni,\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"Shrifal Siddhanath,\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"Upamati Bhava Prapancha Katha,\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"Shri Uttaradhyaya Vritti,\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"Tirtha Vandana Stotra,\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"Vimal Prabandh,\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"Tirthmala,\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"365 Shri Parshwa Jin Nammala,\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"Shri Shankheshwar Parshwanath Chhand,\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"Shri Bhinmal Stavan,\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"Shri Parshwanath Nammala,\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"Chaitya Paripati,\\\\\\\" and others.\\\"}]\\n2c:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"15\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"Hymn of Praise: O Lord, you showed a miracle to humble the pride of Ghazikhan; you are the God of Bhinmal, who broke the fear that threatened the sangh; break also the fear born of my own delusion, as I meditate upon you. \\\\\\\"With loving devotion I bow in reverence to Shri Bhaybhanjan Parshwa.\\\\\\\"\\\"}]\\n2d:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"16\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"Chanting Mantra: Om Hreem Arham Shri Bhaybhanjan Parshwanathaya Namah.\\\"}]\\n2e:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"17\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"Trust: Shri Bhaybhanjan Parshwanath Shwetambar Jain Trust, Hathiyon ki Pol, Post: Bhinmal, District: Jalore, State: Rajasthan – 343029, Ind\"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,\"ia. Phone: 02969-221190, Mobile: 9461132192.\\\"}]\\n\"])</script></body></html>","rscData":"","segmentData":{"/_tree":"","/_full":"","/$d$lang/tirtha/$d$slug/__PAGE__":"","/$d$lang/tirtha/$d$slug":"","/$d$lang/tirtha":"","/$d$lang":"","/_index":"","/_head":""},"headers":{"x-nextjs-stale-time":"300","x-nextjs-prerender":"1","x-next-cache-tags":"_N_T_/layout,_N_T_/[lang]/layout,_N_T_/[lang]/tirtha/layout,_N_T_/[lang]/tirtha/[slug]/layout,_N_T_/[lang]/tirtha/[slug]/page,_N_T_/en/tirtha/tirtha-089"},"segmentPaths":["/_tree","/_full","/$d$lang/tirtha/$d$slug/__PAGE__","/$d$lang/tirtha/$d$slug","/$d$lang/tirtha","/$d$lang","/_index","/_head"],"revalidate":60,"cacheControl":{"revalidate":60,"expire":31536000}}}